  "research_note": "THE PALMER HOUSE, built by T-3688 for the 1871 scene: Potter Palmer's first hotel, built in 1869-70 at the north-west corner of State and Quincy Streets, eight storeys with 'handsome stone fronts', opened in September 1870 (Andreas vol. 2, p. 509). Built to Andreas's engraving of it. It was the last first-class hotel standing at four in the morning of 9 October 1871, and fell after daylight.",
